effective-potential-with-angular-momentu.symmetry_origin:
The concept of the effective potential arises from the application of conservation laws in systems with central forces. For a central force, the force vector is always directed towards or away from a fixed point, and its magnitude depends only on the radial distance. This symmetry leads to the conservation of angular momentum (
 $l$
 ). By expressing the total energy in polar coordinates and using the conservation of angular momentum to eliminate the angular velocity, the radial component of the motion can be described by an effective potential that includes the centrifugal term.
